{
  "item": "Bahamut01",
  "mu_name": "Bahamut",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain _enum.h:4420 MONSTER_BAHAMUT (45), drawn as MONSTER_MODEL_BAHAMUT = 33 (_enum.h:4183), so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster34.bmd. OpenMU Version075 Maps/Atlans.cs:405-406 names breed 45 'Bahamut'. docs/atlans-port.md Part B 4.",
  "world": "atlans",
  "object_type": 45,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 33,
    "scale": 0.6
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13812-13816, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_BAHAMUT: OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_BAHAMUT); CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_BAHAMUT, ...); Scale = 0.6f. No weapon. Every frame it trails four bubbles and four BITMAP_BLOOD + 1 from bone 2 (:2002-2012), not drawn yet. The Great Bahamut (51) is this body at 1.0 with a smoke trail.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, exported with --actions=all. 35 bones. MONSTER_MODEL_BAHAMUT sets no BoneHead and no PlaySpeed of its own (ZzzOpenData.cpp:3639-3643).",
  "sheets": {
    "fs00": "bahamut_fs00.png",
    "fs01": "bahamut_fs01.png",
    "fs02": "bahamut_fs02.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Three sheets out of Data/Monster beside the model, decoded under a bahamut_ prefix: fs00.OZJ (256x128, the body, 350 triangles) -- a red-brown scaled fish with a toothed head and teal fins; fs01.OZT (128x128, 38) -- the spined fin rays, its own alpha a real mask; fs02.OZJ (3x3 white, 8 triangles), the eyes' glint.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "fs00": "chitin",
    "fs01": "leather",
    "fs02": "chitin"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "As the Budge Dragon's: the scaled hide is a shell and reads a little glossy (chitin), the fin rays a membrane, duller (leather). The eyes take the body's.",
  "soft_alpha": [
    "leather"
  ],
  "soft_alpha_from": "The fin rays' membrane (fs01.OZT, the leather islands): MU draws every sheet with an alpha channel tested AND blended (EnableAlphaTest, ZzzOpenglUtil.cpp:366-393; BMD::RenderMesh, ZzzBMD.cpp:1542-1545), so the membrane at a third to four fifths alpha is seen through and the rays stand solid. Cut at the quarter alone, it drew as solid cards (the user, 2026-10-04: 'work on transparency issues for monster fins').",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3639-3643: SetMonsterSound(..., 130, 130, 131, 131, 130), offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1 = 210 -- 340 BAHAMUT1 (mBahamut1.wav) to move and die, 341 to attack and flinch. 341 is SOUND_MONSTER_YETI1___ (DSPlaySound.h:283), which nothing loads: the arm loads mYeti1.wav into SOUND_MONSTER_YETI1 (278) instead, so MuMain's Bahamut swings silent. mYeti1 is what the arm means, and is used. Wired as bahamut_* in sounds.json.",
  "islands_from": "25 islands for 396 triangles. Island 0 is the body (306, fs00), chitin; islands 1-16 are its teeth, eight mirrored pairs of three triangles in fs00's head corner, bone; 17-23 the fin rays (fs01), leather; 24 the eyes (fs02's white), chitin. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default (islands.py never reads sheet_materials).",
